Subject: [PATCH 52/62] verimark: cleanup IT diagnostic logs + decline
 delete-IT cleanly
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase-4 closure of the IT runtime work :

- Demote temp fp_warn diagnostics added during the 0x96 03 commit
  hunt back to fp_dbg / fp_info :
    verify: vfy_cb_match entry log → removed
    verify: positive verdict full TUID dump → trimmed to fp_info
    verify: attempt %d no-match → fp_dbg
    verify: AFTER_POLL / MATCH transitions → fp_dbg
    enroll: RESOLVE_TUID counters → fp_dbg, no full TUID dump
    verimark: IT enroll sending 0x96 03 with %zu-byte payload → fp_dbg

- verimark_delete : IT branch returns FP_DEVICE_ERROR_NOT_SUPPORTED
  with a precise message pointing at /var/lib/fprint/<user>/ for
  host-side reset. The IT delete opcode is 0xA4 with a 1-byte sub-
  factor selector (≠ DT 0xa3 + TUID) ; the FpFinger → byte mapping
  hasn't been runtime-captured yet and sending a wrong byte risks a
  full firmware-side wipe. Documented as a known limitation in the
  CHANGELOG and ROADMAP.

13/13 standalone tests still green. Full libfprint build clean.
Runtime IT path : enroll-completed + verify-match validated 2026-06-07.
